## Gotcha worth keeping

`nix build` with TWO installables and TWO `-o` flags
(`nix build .#a -o result-a .#b -o result-b`) does NOT create both symlinks —
one is left pointing at a previous build, and the other can be missing entirely.
That cost an hour of chasing "stale" publishes that were really a stale symlink.
Build one output per invocation. (`--refresh` is NOT needed: nix picks up
dirty-tree edits fine — verified directly.)
